  "name": "Gray-Scott Selection: environments",
  "description": "Gray-Scott Selection with each founder's square also painted as its environment, and a stronger seed bank (trait_eps 0.01): a trace of b everywhere carrying the local painted traits, which mixes into the thin leading edge of any lineage colonising that ground. Spots keep dying and being reborn; lineages spread across the squares and compete, while the environment keeps feeding local traits back in, so diversity lasts (3–5 lineages above 2% for 300k steps in the lab) and the population drifts slowly towards lower kill. Tint = each spot's own feed. Try: repaint a square's F/k (Background target) to change its environment; set trait_eps back to 0.001 to see blending wipe out diversity.",
